  "looseSpelling": {
    "about": "Which typed spellings spell a word out, for ranking (the engine's Romanisation::relaxed). Vowel length only: Sinhala keeps its dental and retroflex t and d apart in writing (ත ට, ද ඩ), but typists don't, so the skeleton folds th to t; no letter is read as another here.",
